WEBVTT

1
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.201
You? You again! Get out!

2
00:03:43.482 --> 00:03:45.763
Do what I told you.
Get out!

3
00:03:53.416 --> 00:03:56.485
Go on! Run! I'll teach you
to keep away from me!

4
00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.953
Run!

5
00:04:05.439 --> 00:04:06.627
Papa!

6
00:04:09.365 --> 00:04:11.564
You filthy dog!

7
00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.372
You'll settle with me!

8
00:04:35.691 --> 00:04:37.025
Let's go.

9
00:06:34.693 --> 00:06:36.560
Welcome to you, stranger.

10
00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:40.584
My name is Juan de Dios.
I am the bell ringer.

11
00:06:41.217 --> 00:06:43.898
Why are you here?
To see the Rojos?

12
00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.656
No, not the Rojos.
Is it the Baxters, maybe?

13
00:06:47.723 --> 00:06:49.424
No, maybe not
even the Baxters.

14
00:06:49.492 --> 00:06:52.527
You want to get rich? Well, for
that you have come to the right place,

15
00:06:52.595 --> 00:06:54.206
if you use your head.

16
00:06:54.596 --> 00:06:58.359
That's because everybody here
has become very rich,

17
00:06:58.445 --> 00:06:59.801
or else they are dead.

18
00:07:00.203 --> 00:07:04.255
What you want to buy?
Some guns? Liquor?

19
00:07:04.513 --> 00:07:07.332
You don't buy. You sell.
You sell lead in exchange for gold.

20
00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.775
You will get rich here,
or you'll be killed.

21
00:07:11.129 --> 00:07:13.379
Juan de Dios tolls the bell
once again.

22
00:07:29.634 --> 00:07:31.500
<i>Saludos, amigo!</i>

23
00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:35.353
It's not smart to go
wandering so far from home.

24
00:07:37.599 --> 00:07:39.731
I reckon
he picked the wrong trail.

25
00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:41.769
Or he could have
picked the wrong town.

26
00:07:41.816 --> 00:07:44.487
His big mistake, I think,
was getting born.

27
00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:48.142
If you want any work,
looking like that

28
00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:50.648
you could try being a scarecrow.

29
00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:54.906
Oh, no, the crows are liable
to scare him, maybe.

30
00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.891
Hello.

31
00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:26.821
You can't get rich like that.

32
00:08:26.915 --> 00:08:30.101
At most, you will only
succeed in being killed.

33
00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.380
With all of the trouble
we have, all we needed was you.

34
00:08:36.503 --> 00:08:39.777
What are you looking for?
Food and something to drink.

35
00:08:40.006 --> 00:08:43.244
Water's over there.
No, no water.

36
00:08:43.549 --> 00:08:45.344
Eating and drinking
and killing.

37
00:08:45.412 --> 00:08:48.961
That's all you can do,
just like the rest of your kind.

38
00:08:49.116 --> 00:08:53.084
By the way,
you'll have to mark this up.

39
00:08:53.387 --> 00:08:58.097
I know. You have no money.
After all, you just got into town.

40
00:08:58.355 --> 00:09:00.493
But if you don't mind
doing a little killing,

41
00:09:00.561 --> 00:09:04.142
you will have no trouble finding
someone eager to pay you.

42
00:09:08.902 --> 00:09:10.210
Hmm.

43
00:09:10.404 --> 00:09:13.583
My roulette wheel.
That, too, was bartered.

44
00:09:14.642 --> 00:09:16.842
No one ever comes here
to play.

45
00:09:17.027 --> 00:09:20.246
We spend our time here
between funerals and burials.

46
00:09:20.448 --> 00:09:22.782
Never saw a town
as dead as this one.

47
00:09:26.987 --> 00:09:28.929
You will never see another
like it.

48
00:09:29.139 --> 00:09:32.724
What's wrong with the place?
We've had too many killings.

49
00:09:33.263 --> 00:09:34.715
You have seen the women?

50
00:09:34.878 --> 00:09:36.946
None of them are women.
They're widows.

51
00:09:37.152 --> 00:09:38.948
The place has only widows.

52
00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:41.551
Here you can only gain respect
by killing other men.

53
00:09:41.697 --> 00:09:43.553
So nobody works anymore.

54
00:09:46.223 --> 00:09:48.561
Seems somebody doesn't
share your opinion.

55
00:09:48.792 --> 00:09:50.389
Yes.

56
00:09:59.736 --> 00:10:01.915
Know why Piripero
looked you over?

57
00:10:02.172 --> 00:10:04.140
To take your measurements.

58
00:10:04.375 --> 00:10:06.542
He is so experienced
he can do it with a glance.

59
00:10:06.694 --> 00:10:08.544
You will be a customer.

60
00:10:09.679 --> 00:10:11.547
Don't laugh. I'm not joking.

61
00:10:11.615 --> 00:10:15.269
I want to warn you that those murderers
will make a corpse out of you one day.

62
00:10:15.419 --> 00:10:17.659
That's why I want you
to get out of here.

63
00:10:18.198 --> 00:10:20.704
You don't want to stay
in this cemetery.

64
00:10:21.337 --> 00:10:23.292
Finish up and get out.

65
00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:27.997
I told you
I can't pay you.

66
00:10:28.482 --> 00:10:30.075
Be my guest,

67
00:10:30.661 --> 00:10:33.419
but get out of San Miguel,
will you?

68
00:10:35.932 --> 00:10:37.385
Where does that lead?

69
00:10:37.854 --> 00:10:39.353
The balcony.

70
00:10:41.696 --> 00:10:44.447
Why are you going there? Hey.

71
00:10:45.148 --> 00:10:46.816
To have a look.

72
00:10:46.967 --> 00:10:49.084
Things always look different
from higher up.

73
00:10:49.333 --> 00:10:50.886
But nothing's up there.

74
00:10:51.184 --> 00:10:52.822
Go ahead and get out!

75
00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:03.039
Who are they?

76
00:11:03.929 --> 00:11:07.256
Bandits.
Bandits and smugglers.

77
00:11:07.865 --> 00:11:09.238
They come down
from Texas.

78
00:11:09.411 --> 00:11:12.341
They cross the frontier to
stock up on guns and liquor.

79
00:11:12.644 --> 00:11:14.343
The cost is much less here.

80
00:11:14.518 --> 00:11:17.868
Then they go back and sell the
guns and liquor to the Indians.

81
00:11:19.583 --> 00:11:22.460
Any town that sells guns and
liquor has gotta be a rich one.

82
00:11:22.624 --> 00:11:25.521
Not the town,
only those who buy and sell,

83
00:11:25.589 --> 00:11:28.270
and the bosses are the ones
who clean up.

84
00:11:28.481 --> 00:11:31.794
Yeah? Somebody has to run the place.
Every town has a boss.

85
00:11:32.066 --> 00:11:34.397
That's true, but when
there are two around,

86
00:11:34.619 --> 00:11:36.915
then I'd say that
there is one too many.

87
00:11:37.173 --> 00:11:38.766
Two bosses?

88
00:11:39.633 --> 00:11:41.273
Very interesting.

89
00:11:41.405 --> 00:11:43.381
Interesting is right.

90
00:11:43.841 --> 00:11:46.409
The Rojos boys, three brothers
who sell liquor.

91
00:11:46.477 --> 00:11:50.691
And then there's the Baxters,
big gun merchants.

92
00:11:51.534 --> 00:11:55.658
If I'm not mistaken, you already
met Baxter's gang, didn't you?

93
00:11:55.886 --> 00:11:57.462
Yeah, we met.

94
00:11:57.743 --> 00:12:01.891
But you're lucky. They don't usually
limit their fire to the mule.

95
00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:04.959
A man leaves his own land and
looks around for any reason,

96
00:12:05.029 --> 00:12:09.165
Juan de Dios tolls the bell and
Piripero sells another coffin.

97
00:12:09.233 --> 00:12:10.666
Two bosses.

98
00:12:13.346 --> 00:12:17.539
They've enlisted all the scum that hangs
around both sides of the frontier,

99
00:12:17.674 --> 00:12:19.808
and they pay in dollars.

100
00:12:22.694 --> 00:12:24.334
The Baxters over there.

101
00:12:25.505 --> 00:12:27.051
The Rojos there.

102
00:12:28.218 --> 00:12:29.718
Me right in the middle.

103
00:12:29.786 --> 00:12:31.198
Where you do what?

104
00:12:33.257 --> 00:12:35.251
Crazy bell ringer
was right.

105
00:12:35.492 --> 00:12:37.922
There's money to be made
in a place like this.

106
00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:42.565
If you're thinking what I suspect,
I tell you, don't try it.

107
00:12:43.779 --> 00:12:45.957
Which one of the two
is the stronger?

108
00:12:46.332 --> 00:12:48.909
Which one of them
is stronger?

109
00:12:49.401 --> 00:12:52.939
Well, the Rojos,
especially Ramon.

110
00:13:04.114 --> 00:13:08.519
Don Miguel Rojo,
I want to talk to you.

111
00:13:09.057 --> 00:13:12.431
Don Miguel, I hear
you're hiring on men.

112
00:13:13.181 --> 00:13:15.570
Well, I might
just be available.

113
00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:20.233
I gotta tell you
before you hire me,

114
00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:25.107
I don't work cheap.

115
00:13:40.732 --> 00:13:42.508
Get three coffins ready.

116
00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:12.899
Listen, stranger.
Didn't you get the idea?

117
00:14:12.992 --> 00:14:15.382
We don't like to see
bad boys like you in town.

118
00:14:15.476 --> 00:14:17.116
Go get your mule.

119
00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:20.232
You let him
get away from you?

120
00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:23.137
That's what I want to talk
to you about.

121
00:14:23.488 --> 00:14:25.409
He's feeling real bad.

122
00:14:26.838 --> 00:14:28.080
My mule.

123
00:14:28.322 --> 00:14:32.133
He got all riled up when you men
fired those shots at his feet.

124
00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.563
Hey, are you making
some kind of joke?

125
00:14:37.631 --> 00:14:39.653
Mmm-mmm. No.

126
00:14:40.145 --> 00:14:42.722
See, I understand you men
were just playing around.

127
00:14:42.839 --> 00:14:45.065
But the mule...
He just doesn't get it.

128
00:14:45.338 --> 00:14:47.773
Of course, if you were
to all apologize...

129
00:14:59.886 --> 00:15:02.097
I don't think it's nice,
you laughing.

130
00:15:06.103 --> 00:15:08.563
You see, my mule
don't like people laughing.

131
00:15:09.875 --> 00:15:12.546
He gets the crazy idea
you're laughing at him.

132
00:15:13.033 --> 00:15:16.107
Now, if you apologize,
like I know you're going to,

133
00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.949
I might convince him that
you really didn't mean it.

134
00:15:48.735 --> 00:15:51.003
I saw the whole thing.
You killed all four of them.

135
00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:55.161
You'll pay all right.
You'll be strung up.

136
00:15:57.879 --> 00:15:59.211
Who are you?

137
00:15:59.636 --> 00:16:01.229
Don't fire a shot.

138
00:16:03.049 --> 00:16:06.477
I'm John Baxter, sheriff.

139
00:16:07.904 --> 00:16:12.123
Yeah? Well, if you're the sheriff, you
better get these men underground.

140
00:16:25.852 --> 00:16:28.390
My mistake. Four coffins.

141
00:16:46.469 --> 00:16:48.319
I told you I wasn't cheap,

142
00:16:48.578 --> 00:16:50.967
but I think you'll find
it's worth your while.

143
00:16:51.047 --> 00:16:53.895
...97, 98, 99, 100.

144
00:16:54.817 --> 00:16:56.519
The rest
when you're all done.

145
00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.049
When do I start?

146
00:16:59.989 --> 00:17:02.446
I'm not in a hurry,
at least for the moment.

147
00:17:02.962 --> 00:17:04.460
I'd say with
four less Baxters,

148
00:17:04.527 --> 00:17:07.028
right now is as good a time
to start as any.

149
00:17:07.202 --> 00:17:11.233
In a few days I hear there will be a troop
of cavalry passing through San Miguel.

150
00:17:11.349 --> 00:17:15.168
I wouldn't want the military sticking
their long noses into our business.

151
00:17:16.739 --> 00:17:18.963
You seem to be well informed.

152
00:17:20.603 --> 00:17:25.687
In these parts, a man's life often
depends on a mere scrap of information.

153
00:17:26.866 --> 00:17:29.740
This thing couldn't have been
very useful to its owner.

154
00:17:32.288 --> 00:17:36.440
My brother Ramon did that. He often
uses it for target practice.

155
00:17:36.659 --> 00:17:40.001
With a gun in his hand,
no one stands in his way.

156
00:17:40.763 --> 00:17:43.422
The suit of armor is
one of his favorite targets,

157
00:17:43.533 --> 00:17:46.186
naturally, when he does not
have anything better to shoot.

158
00:17:47.475 --> 00:17:51.294
Well, I'll be kind of curious
to meet this brother of yours.

159
00:17:52.375 --> 00:17:53.660
Ah.

160
00:17:54.076 --> 00:17:57.432
This is Chico, one
of the most trusted of my men.

161
00:17:58.014 --> 00:18:00.899
Follow him. He will bring you
to your room.

162
00:18:01.183 --> 00:18:03.148
I would like you
to feel at home.

163
00:18:03.786 --> 00:18:06.944
Well, I never found home
that great, but let's go.

164
00:18:25.391 --> 00:18:26.740
Who's that?

165
00:18:27.138 --> 00:18:31.168
Her name's Marisol.
You just forget about her.

166
00:18:34.433 --> 00:18:36.601
This one will be your room.

167
00:19:07.767 --> 00:19:09.520
You gave him $100.

168
00:19:09.769 --> 00:19:12.570
We never pay that much.

169
00:19:12.638 --> 00:19:14.873
Can you explain to me
why you have taken him on?

170
00:19:14.941 --> 00:19:18.750
To have that filthy gringo around the
house and to give him $100 besides?

171
00:19:18.914 --> 00:19:21.233
We have never paid anybody
so much.

172
00:19:21.698 --> 00:19:24.373
You cannot leave someone like that
to do what he wants around here.

173
00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:28.262
He's capable of doing anything. And
I want law and order in this place.

174
00:19:29.269 --> 00:19:33.322
If that is all you want,
there is a much cheaper way.

175
00:19:33.908 --> 00:19:35.618
Just snuff him out.

176
00:19:38.147 --> 00:19:39.906
And who will be the one? You?

177
00:19:39.999 --> 00:19:41.686
Yes, why not?

178
00:19:42.218 --> 00:19:43.584
A shot in his back,

179
00:19:43.654 --> 00:19:46.589
then you would have him out
of the way in no time at all.

180
00:19:47.958 --> 00:19:50.753
Listen, I could do it easily
right now.

181
00:19:52.041 --> 00:19:56.431
He won't be expecting it,
and I'd get back the $100.

182
00:19:59.368 --> 00:20:03.005
You're stupid, Esteban!
Even if you are my brother!

183
00:20:03.673 --> 00:20:06.875
A bullet in the back, eh?
And it is ended!

184
00:20:07.012 --> 00:20:09.518
And what happens if your hand
should tremble slightly?

185
00:20:09.645 --> 00:20:11.182
And he's only been hurt?

186
00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:15.938
And with the cavalry arriving in town
and that Yankee so quick on the draw.

187
00:20:16.125 --> 00:20:18.866
I was only thinking... You
mustn't think of anything!

188
00:20:19.194 --> 00:20:21.115
You let me
do the thinking instead.

189
00:20:21.303 --> 00:20:25.994
Go and see the <i>americano</i>. Just ask him
if he needs anything and make friends.

190
00:20:27.563 --> 00:20:29.573
Get one thing clear
in that head of yours.

191
00:20:29.643 --> 00:20:33.151
This is going to be a quiet
town until Ramon gets back!

192
00:20:34.454 --> 00:20:37.789
Is that clear? A quiet town.

193
00:20:51.304 --> 00:20:53.774
I am Esteban Rojo.
My brother asked me to...

194
00:20:59.443 --> 00:21:00.849
What are you doing?

195
00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:03.684
Moving.

196
00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.968
But didn't you know
all our men live here with us?

197
00:21:09.539 --> 00:21:14.695
That's all very cozy, but I don't
find you men all that appealing.

198
00:21:14.977 --> 00:21:18.959
Besides, your brother said he didn't
have any need for me anymore right now.

199
00:21:42.996 --> 00:21:44.753
Halt!

200
00:21:46.627 --> 00:21:49.228
- Sergeant?
- Yes, <i>Capitan</i>?

201
00:21:49.946 --> 00:21:52.391
Tell the men we'll be spending
tonight here in this place.

202
00:21:52.582 --> 00:21:54.683
Arrange it so they can
pick up the supplies here.

203
00:21:54.827 --> 00:21:57.285
Also, double the guard in order
to watch the stagecoach there.

204
00:21:57.428 --> 00:21:58.903
Yes, sir.

205
00:21:59.958 --> 00:22:02.474
What do you suppose they're
carrying in that coach?

206
00:22:02.542 --> 00:22:04.209
It'd be easy
to find out.

207
00:22:04.432 --> 00:22:06.945
Get up close to it and take a
little look at what's in it.

208
00:22:07.103 --> 00:22:09.633
If they fire at you,
you know it's gold.

209
00:22:10.383 --> 00:22:12.304
Not a bad idea.

210
00:22:38.356 --> 00:22:39.996
Looking for anything?

211
00:22:41.495 --> 00:22:42.690
Hello.

212
00:22:43.182 --> 00:22:44.658
Get out of here, Yankee.

213
00:22:59.137 --> 00:23:00.730
Why aren't you sleeping?

214
00:23:01.854 --> 00:23:04.689
When I see you staring
like that, it bothers me.

215
00:23:05.486 --> 00:23:08.602
I still keep wondering
what was in that stagecoach.

216
00:23:08.836 --> 00:23:11.483
It's something they seem
to think is very important.

217
00:23:11.999 --> 00:23:15.700
I asked a few questions of the
captain and almost was arrested.

218
00:23:17.333 --> 00:23:19.004
Who's Marisol?

219
00:23:20.602 --> 00:23:23.033
You better get some sleep.
You need it.

220
00:23:23.739 --> 00:23:26.009
It's much too dangerous,
even for you.

221
00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:30.545
All I did is ask
who she was.

222
00:23:31.795 --> 00:23:33.318
She is a woman.

223
00:23:33.740 --> 00:23:36.051
And Ramon's madly in love
with her.

224
00:23:36.153 --> 00:23:37.910
Does that make it clear
to you?

225
00:23:40.873 --> 00:23:43.884
Everybody in this town
talks about Ramon.

226
00:23:44.095 --> 00:23:45.875
Kind of curious
to meet him.

227
00:23:46.508 --> 00:23:50.327
If you are smart, you will try to stay
clear of Ramon as long as possible.

228
00:23:57.285 --> 00:24:01.310
There are the soldiers.
They are moving on very quietly.

229
00:24:06.115 --> 00:24:07.570
Strange.

230
00:24:08.296 --> 00:24:10.030
They're headed
for the frontier.

231
00:24:15.067 --> 00:24:16.358
Tell me,

232
00:24:18.932 --> 00:24:21.129
is that the way
you go to bed every night?

233
00:24:22.329 --> 00:24:24.766
Don't worry.
I didn't dirty the sheets.

234
00:24:26.619 --> 00:24:28.920
No, wait. I'm coming, too.

235
00:24:28.987 --> 00:24:32.263
I want to see for myself how you're
going to get yourself in trouble.

236
00:24:32.567 --> 00:24:34.231
All right. All right.
Go ahead.

237
00:25:19.755 --> 00:25:22.424
It's like playing cowboys
and Indians.

238
00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:28.479
- Captain.
- Welcome, Lieutenant.

239
00:25:29.648 --> 00:25:31.606
There is your gold
as promised.

240
00:25:32.050 --> 00:25:35.565
I hope the guns you will be giving us
will be equally useful to our army.

241
00:25:35.721 --> 00:25:39.090
Rest assured, Captain. We'll
check them over together.

242
00:27:12.902 --> 00:27:15.570
Get their clothes on again,
and hurry.

243
00:27:17.272 --> 00:27:19.207
Be sure to place them
around right.

244
00:27:19.304 --> 00:27:21.600
Remember. They died
fighting among themselves.

245
00:27:39.850 --> 00:27:41.232
Rubio!

246
00:27:46.986 --> 00:27:49.187
There. It's Ramon.

247
00:28:03.185 --> 00:28:05.176
This is my brother Ramon.

248
00:28:05.855 --> 00:28:07.519
I think I mentioned him.

249
00:28:07.957 --> 00:28:09.758
Everybody talks about Ramon.

250
00:28:09.861 --> 00:28:13.821
And many speak of you, too,
my dear brother included.

251
00:28:14.172 --> 00:28:18.061
Well, I hope
they say nice things.

252
00:28:19.045 --> 00:28:20.468
Did you have a good trip?

253
00:28:21.253 --> 00:28:22.817
It was tiring.

254
00:28:23.255 --> 00:28:25.863
It was terribly hot
on the road during the day.

255
00:28:26.391 --> 00:28:30.501
And stagecoaches are an
uncomfortable way to travel.

256
00:28:30.746 --> 00:28:33.969
Well, I'm sure you'll be
in great shape in no time.

257
00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:36.944
The <i>americano</i> cannot
wait to get into action.

258
00:28:37.653 --> 00:28:41.067
I am sorry. He's going
to be a disappointed man.

259
00:28:41.255 --> 00:28:42.332
How's that?

260
00:28:42.426 --> 00:28:44.394
The Baxters
accepted the invitation.

261
00:28:44.511 --> 00:28:46.456
They'll come tonight,
Don Miguel.

262
00:28:47.229 --> 00:28:49.384
The Baxters coming here?
You must be out of your head.

263
00:28:49.498 --> 00:28:52.383
Chico followed my orders. I
told him to invite them here.

264
00:28:52.601 --> 00:28:54.491
Ramon, what is this?

265
00:28:56.071 --> 00:28:58.440
I have found out many things
when I was traveling,

266
00:28:58.507 --> 00:29:01.778
and I have decided
that it's very stupid,

267
00:29:02.044 --> 00:29:06.147
to just keep on shooting at each
other and without any results.

268
00:29:06.393 --> 00:29:08.267
You've gone
out of your mind, Ramon.

269
00:29:08.684 --> 00:29:11.547
No, I have come
to my senses, Esteban.

270
00:29:12.062 --> 00:29:13.421
Believe me.

271
00:29:14.241 --> 00:29:15.423
Trust me.

272
00:29:16.654 --> 00:29:18.827
Life can be so precious.

273
00:29:19.021 --> 00:29:22.207
It's foolish to risk
losing it every minute, no?

274
00:29:23.940 --> 00:29:26.541
There's plenty of space
for everybody in this town.

275
00:29:26.845 --> 00:29:28.392
Even Baxters.

276
00:29:29.750 --> 00:29:31.625
For this reason,

277
00:29:33.171 --> 00:29:35.936
I've decided to hang
my gun up on the wall.

278
00:29:36.712 --> 00:29:38.864
I think that
Ramon has the right idea.

279
00:29:38.981 --> 00:29:42.191
I, too, am getting tired of these killings.
They must stop.

280
00:29:43.714 --> 00:29:46.954
This is all
very, very touching.

281
00:29:47.743 --> 00:29:49.430
You mean
you don't admire peace?

282
00:29:49.828 --> 00:29:52.874
It's not real easy to like
something you know nothing about.

283
00:29:53.952 --> 00:29:57.465
Stay in San Miguel and you may
just profit from the experience.

284
00:29:57.606 --> 00:30:00.702
No, thanks. I'll be moving on.

285
00:30:07.076 --> 00:30:09.555
Here's your money,
Don Miguel.

286
00:30:09.719 --> 00:30:11.874
I only used
a small amount of it.

287
00:30:12.085 --> 00:30:15.716
I don't like to take money
unless I feel I've earned it.

288
00:30:17.486 --> 00:30:20.261
Now, why are you so hasty?
You should stay here.

289
00:30:20.917 --> 00:30:22.955
You might enjoy
dining with us tonight.

290
00:30:23.541 --> 00:30:26.985
You see, the Baxters have four men
in the cemetery on account of me.

291
00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:30.031
I don't think
they'd appreciate my presence.

292
00:30:37.857 --> 00:30:41.159
I don't like that <i>americano</i>.
He's too smart to be just a hired fighter.

293
00:30:41.487 --> 00:30:43.094
At shooting a pistol
no one can touch him.

294
00:30:43.162 --> 00:30:44.181
I can see that.

295
00:30:44.275 --> 00:30:48.166
When someone with that face works with
his gun, you may count on two things.

296
00:30:48.351 --> 00:30:51.169
He's fast on the trigger,
but he's also intelligent.

297
00:30:51.350 --> 00:30:53.927
That makes him too dangerous
for you, I think, my brothers.

298
00:30:54.068 --> 00:30:56.807
And now that he's gone, will you
please explain that silly nonsense

299
00:30:56.876 --> 00:30:59.433
about hanging up your gun and
making up with the Baxters?

300
00:31:00.534 --> 00:31:02.213
Is it possible, old fellow,

301
00:31:02.549 --> 00:31:05.407
that you'll never be able to reach
any conclusions on your own?

302
00:31:06.320 --> 00:31:09.390
Don't you think our government and the
<i>americanos</i> will find those bodies,

303
00:31:09.483 --> 00:31:11.639
and then start
an investigation?

304
00:31:11.756 --> 00:31:13.091
They'll investigate,
all right,

305
00:31:13.359 --> 00:31:17.051
and we'll be quiet
and peacefully abide our time.

306
00:31:17.596 --> 00:31:20.565
We know nothing about the
massacre at the Rio Bravo, eh?

307
00:31:21.367 --> 00:31:23.667
I arranged for the bodies
to be lying,

308
00:31:23.798 --> 00:31:26.258
as if both companies
killed each other.

309
00:31:27.006 --> 00:31:29.467
But do you think
they'll believe it?

310
00:31:29.674 --> 00:31:31.904
Yes, I think so.

311
00:31:32.278 --> 00:31:34.379
Because if they don't
find some guilty party,

312
00:31:34.481 --> 00:31:37.573
it would be a pretty good reason
to call off the investigation.

313
00:31:37.849 --> 00:31:40.584
Yes, but what
about the Baxters?

314
00:31:40.652 --> 00:31:42.376
The Baxters?

315
00:31:43.522 --> 00:31:46.288
They want nothing more
than to live in peace.

316
00:31:46.491 --> 00:31:48.819
We'll let them have
their own way for a while.

317
00:31:48.994 --> 00:31:50.388
So forget about the Baxters.

318
00:31:50.482 --> 00:31:54.558
We'll take care of them later
when the investigation finishes.

319
00:32:00.956 --> 00:32:03.508
That was a fine idea
that you had.

320
00:32:03.693 --> 00:32:05.429
What was it again?

321
00:32:05.851 --> 00:32:07.866
Ah, yes, yes, yes.

322
00:32:08.431 --> 00:32:13.535
The Baxters on one side.
The Rojos on the other.

323
00:32:14.903 --> 00:32:16.792
And you'd be in the middle.

324
00:32:17.635 --> 00:32:20.095
The only problem is that
they've joined up.

325
00:32:22.813 --> 00:32:26.772
Now you are without a job, and you don't
have money to pay me what you owe me.

326
00:32:27.049 --> 00:32:30.552
There is only one thing for you to do.
Leave here immediately.

327
00:32:30.685 --> 00:32:32.465
I will forget about
what you owe me.

328
00:32:32.816 --> 00:32:36.401
And you leave San Miguel and never
come back for the rest of your days.

329
00:32:36.625 --> 00:32:40.454
Joe, I have prepared the wagon
the way you asked me to.

330
00:32:40.548 --> 00:32:43.945
It's sitting out in the back
here with two empty coffins.

331
00:32:44.226 --> 00:32:45.842
What are you up to?

332
00:32:46.100 --> 00:32:47.880
Are you changing
your profession?

333
00:32:48.420 --> 00:32:50.528
If you want to go on living,
you'd better.

334
00:32:50.889 --> 00:32:54.347
In my opinion,
you'll make a fine pallbearer.

335
00:32:56.595 --> 00:32:58.728
Close this place
and come with me, huh?

336
00:32:58.830 --> 00:33:03.038
Oh, close up?
It's done. Where are we going?

337
00:33:03.201 --> 00:33:06.318
I'd like to know where we are
going, or is it a secret?

338
00:33:07.539 --> 00:33:11.309
Down by the river. Have a look
at some corpses down there.

339
00:33:55.370 --> 00:33:57.977
The Rojos say, "Come to
dinner," and we must go.

340
00:33:58.273 --> 00:34:00.203
But I don't like it at all,

341
00:34:01.046 --> 00:34:03.927
even if they've granted all the
guarantees we've demanded.

342
00:34:05.919 --> 00:34:09.527
We'll go along with it,
but don't touch anything.

343
00:34:09.761 --> 00:34:12.549
You mustn't eat.
You mustn't drink.

344
00:34:13.288 --> 00:34:16.954
You just keep your eyes open
and keep your wits about you.

345
00:34:43.469 --> 00:34:45.700
Are you sure
that nobody has seen us?

346
00:34:45.870 --> 00:34:47.808
Only a ghost or two.

347
00:34:47.996 --> 00:34:50.877
Oh, no, no, no. Don't joke
about things like this.

348
00:34:50.971 --> 00:34:53.618
Ghosts are better left
where they are.

349
00:34:55.047 --> 00:34:57.649
You look as though this
place suits you very well.

350
00:34:57.906 --> 00:35:01.326
If you go on like this, you
will soon be here permanently.

351
00:35:14.071 --> 00:35:15.055
I do not understand.

352
00:35:15.125 --> 00:35:19.061
Why is it with all those bodies down by
the river we are just burying these two?

353
00:35:19.271 --> 00:35:21.572
We're not.
We're not gonna bury them.

354
00:35:21.639 --> 00:35:23.606
What do you mean
we're not burying them?

355
00:35:24.168 --> 00:35:26.558
That's right.
We're not gonna bury them.

356
00:35:28.013 --> 00:35:29.313
If we are not going to
bury them,

357
00:35:29.381 --> 00:35:31.806
I would like to know
what we will use them for?

358
00:35:32.651 --> 00:35:35.132
Why are we taking
the trouble to do this?

359
00:35:36.327 --> 00:35:38.690
The dead can be
very useful sometimes.

360
00:35:42.194 --> 00:35:45.042
They've helped me out of
tough spots more than once.

361
00:35:51.470 --> 00:35:53.360
First, they don't talk.

362
00:35:55.726 --> 00:35:59.099
Second, they can be made to look
alive if I manage it right.

363
00:36:01.583 --> 00:36:03.504
And, third...

364
00:36:04.839 --> 00:36:07.017
Well, third, if you shoot
them, there's no worry,

365
00:36:07.085 --> 00:36:08.517
'cause they're dead already.

366
00:36:09.188 --> 00:36:10.462
Understand?

367
00:36:11.390 --> 00:36:13.808
It doesn't make a bit of sense
to me, and I'm getting out.

368
00:36:13.929 --> 00:36:16.010
I'm alive, and I want to remain
with the living, understand?

369
00:36:16.078 --> 00:36:17.979
And when I'm dead, I'll want
to remain with the dead.

370
00:36:18.047 --> 00:36:20.887
I would be unhappy if somebody living
forces me to remain with the living.

371
00:36:20.981 --> 00:36:22.597
I hope that's clear.

372
00:36:23.488 --> 00:36:27.455
And, also, I don't like the idea that
you've placed those bodies there!

373
00:36:27.611 --> 00:36:31.926
The man buried there is the only one who
died of pneumonia in this cursed town!

374
00:36:32.133 --> 00:36:33.843
Take it easy now, will you?

375
00:36:33.937 --> 00:36:36.865
These two friends of ours here
are gonna help me pay your bill.

376
00:36:37.568 --> 00:36:39.044
Get up there!

377
00:37:07.228 --> 00:37:09.964
The only reason they could
have to start a war with us,

378
00:37:10.032 --> 00:37:12.874
would be to kidnap you
from your husband's side.

379
00:37:14.136 --> 00:37:16.154
He's gallant, this Rojo.

380
00:37:16.337 --> 00:37:18.895
I really didn't think him
capable of compliments.

381
00:37:19.293 --> 00:37:23.978
And he's not. All that he says
is false, like his proposals.

382
00:37:24.166 --> 00:37:28.758
You women. If things aren't complicated
for you, you become suspicious.

383
00:37:28.898 --> 00:37:32.717
Yes, because to me,
it just didn't seem right.

384
00:37:32.988 --> 00:37:36.490
It went too smoothly.
I don't trust them.

385
00:37:36.606 --> 00:37:38.949
You'd like to prove me wrong,
wouldn't you?

386
00:37:39.066 --> 00:37:40.683
Always the same thing.

387
00:37:43.166 --> 00:37:45.368
Good night.
Good night.

388
00:38:24.001 --> 00:38:26.180
Don't worry.
I'm not gonna hurt you.

389
00:38:27.140 --> 00:38:30.828
I just want you to know why the Rojos
want to make peace all of a sudden.

390
00:38:32.597 --> 00:38:34.565
You see, there was once
a wagon load of gold

391
00:38:34.633 --> 00:38:37.050
that the soldiers
were taking to the border.

392
00:38:45.394 --> 00:38:47.733
John,
come up here quickly.

393
00:38:54.152 --> 00:38:59.122
Sorry, but when a husband finds
a man in his wife's bedroom,

394
00:38:59.191 --> 00:39:01.392
you're never sure
how he's gonna react.

395
00:39:04.672 --> 00:39:06.991
Give him $500.
How's that?

396
00:39:07.132 --> 00:39:08.819
Give the money to him.

397
00:39:09.651 --> 00:39:12.145
He has an interesting story.
Listen to him.

398
00:39:13.405 --> 00:39:15.402
That's the right idea?
You didn't misunderstand?

399
00:39:15.542 --> 00:39:17.440
I get the wrong idea only
when it suits me.

400
00:39:17.487 --> 00:39:18.743
- Ramon.
- What is it?

401
00:39:18.893 --> 00:39:20.611
The soldiers, the ones
who were escorting the gold...

402
00:39:20.679 --> 00:39:23.367
Two of those soldiers got away. They
are hiding out in the cemetery.

403
00:39:23.515 --> 00:39:26.155
The Baxters.
They're about to capture them.

404
00:39:28.920 --> 00:39:30.864
Rubio! Get the men!

405
00:39:33.441 --> 00:39:35.198
You are well-informed, eh?

406
00:39:35.493 --> 00:39:39.556
A man's life in these parts often
depends on a mere scrap of information.

407
00:39:39.790 --> 00:39:41.548
Your brother's own words.

408
00:39:41.969 --> 00:39:44.501
Tell me. Why are you
doing this for us?

409
00:39:48.073 --> 00:39:49.747
$500.

410
00:39:57.082 --> 00:40:00.009
With these two soldiers
as witnesses against Ramon,

411
00:40:00.118 --> 00:40:03.820
the government will be able to rid the
town of the Rojos and their whole band.

412
00:40:03.968 --> 00:40:06.358
Then San Miguel
will have just one boss.

413
00:40:06.624 --> 00:40:07.824
Hurry!

414
00:40:23.041 --> 00:40:24.491
Let's go!

415
00:40:28.099 --> 00:40:29.294
Coming with us?

416
00:40:29.414 --> 00:40:33.604
Oh, no. When a man's got money in his
pocket, he begins to appreciate peace.

417
00:40:34.705 --> 00:40:35.953
Come on!

418
00:41:45.200 --> 00:41:47.215
Let's leave
the horses here.

419
00:42:10.174 --> 00:42:11.965
Who's there? Come out!

420
00:42:33.954 --> 00:42:35.570
What do you think?

421
00:42:35.991 --> 00:42:37.515
I don't know.

422
00:42:38.335 --> 00:42:40.327
There's something about it
I don't like.

423
00:42:40.513 --> 00:42:43.231
Too still to be wounded.
More like dummies.

424
00:42:43.606 --> 00:42:45.808
Sure, dummies that are
very interesting to the Rojos.

425
00:42:45.925 --> 00:42:47.534
Better hide. Hurry.

426
00:45:02.768 --> 00:45:03.820
What'll we do?

427
00:45:04.033 --> 00:45:06.039
Take two men
and circle around to the side.

428
00:45:06.235 --> 00:45:09.376
Try to keep them busy long enough
for me to get those two down there.

429
00:45:09.515 --> 00:45:12.069
Go on. Go on. Quickly.

430
00:45:49.272 --> 00:45:51.990
Keep me covered. I am going
to take care of those two.

431
00:46:29.498 --> 00:46:33.551
Listen, Baxter! You can
have them now if you like!

432
00:46:33.738 --> 00:46:36.263
Since dead men can't talk!

433
00:46:47.772 --> 00:46:50.255
It seems
they didn't like my joke.

434
00:46:50.747 --> 00:46:53.465
We'll let them go home
in a little while.

435
00:48:37.683 --> 00:48:39.172
Keep this bad boy
as our guest,

436
00:48:39.265 --> 00:48:42.217
only until Baxter leaves San
Miguel and heads for the frontier.

437
00:48:42.358 --> 00:48:43.956
Put him in the cellar.

438
00:48:50.730 --> 00:48:52.397
Esteban, good work.

439
00:48:52.525 --> 00:48:56.635
With Antonio as our prisoner, the
Baxters have to give in to us.

440
00:48:56.766 --> 00:48:58.500
Now we can make
any kind of demand.

441
00:48:58.617 --> 00:49:00.983
Don Miguel! Don Miguel!

442
00:49:05.978 --> 00:49:08.292
What has happened?
Talk, will you?

443
00:49:08.548 --> 00:49:11.183
I don't know,
but somebody shot at me.

444
00:49:11.385 --> 00:49:12.744
Marisol!

445
00:49:14.287 --> 00:49:15.907
Marisol!

446
00:49:16.211 --> 00:49:18.323
Where are you, Marisol?

447
00:49:31.838 --> 00:49:34.639
It's strange how you always
manage to be

448
00:49:34.707 --> 00:49:36.898
in the right place
at the right time.

449
00:49:43.683 --> 00:49:48.003
It's nothing serious. A headache
that will pass. She'll sleep.

450
00:49:53.040 --> 00:49:56.835
Keep your eyes open. She's not to
move from that room. You hear?

451
00:50:04.270 --> 00:50:07.050
I wouldn't mention anything
about me bringing her here.

452
00:50:07.239 --> 00:50:10.189
I wouldn't want the Rojos
to think I was on your side.

453
00:50:10.634 --> 00:50:12.110
Don't be worried.

454
00:50:12.244 --> 00:50:17.241
I'm a woman who's rich enough to
appreciate the men my money can buy.

455
00:50:17.873 --> 00:50:19.351
I've been to talk
to the Rojos.

456
00:50:19.490 --> 00:50:21.620
They'll give back Antonio
in exchange for Marisol.

457
00:50:21.687 --> 00:50:23.496
It'll take place
in the morning.

458
00:50:26.459 --> 00:50:29.353
Very soon
you are going to be rich.

459
00:50:35.210 --> 00:50:38.420
Yeah, and that's not
gonna break my heart.

460
00:52:21.600 --> 00:52:24.770
Where is she? You said
I'd be able to see her!

461
00:52:24.933 --> 00:52:26.304
Where is she?

462
00:52:27.697 --> 00:52:29.707
I wanna see her!

463
00:52:29.776 --> 00:52:31.914
Come back here, Jesus.
Come here. Where is she?

464
00:52:32.149 --> 00:52:34.819
I want to see her!
I want to see her!

465
00:52:34.937 --> 00:52:38.849
Why can't I look at her?
I want to see her!

466
00:52:57.352 --> 00:52:59.911
Go. Go to him, Marisol.

467
00:53:24.747 --> 00:53:26.150
Mama!

468
00:53:29.149 --> 00:53:31.773
Mama!
Jesus!

469
00:53:38.871 --> 00:53:40.111
Mama!

470
00:53:42.447 --> 00:53:43.598
Jesus!

471
00:53:43.665 --> 00:53:45.853
Mama! Mama!

472
00:54:35.984 --> 00:54:37.084
Julio!

473
00:54:38.286 --> 00:54:39.596
Marisol.

474
00:54:41.518 --> 00:54:42.857
Get Julio.

475
00:54:53.352 --> 00:54:55.481
You were warned
to get out of town.

476
00:54:56.395 --> 00:54:59.604
Now I'm gonna make you
pay once and for all.

477
00:55:01.527 --> 00:55:03.411
Let him be.

478
00:55:42.301 --> 00:55:44.562
You better get going.
Ramon's waiting.

479
00:55:48.691 --> 00:55:51.965
And, you, get that kid
home where he belongs.

480
00:56:39.337 --> 00:56:41.126
A pig, that Ramon.

481
00:56:42.242 --> 00:56:44.959
What's Ramon
got to do with them?

482
00:56:45.241 --> 00:56:46.670
You weren't told, eh?

483
00:56:49.645 --> 00:56:51.836
In this part of the world,
the story is very old.

484
00:56:51.904 --> 00:56:54.682
A happy little family
until trouble comes along.

485
00:56:55.207 --> 00:56:56.807
And trouble has
the name of Ramon.

486
00:56:56.875 --> 00:56:59.544
Claiming the husband cheated
at cards, which wasn't true,

487
00:56:59.611 --> 00:57:02.765
he gets the wife
to live with him as hostage.

488
00:57:03.280 --> 00:57:04.592
And the husband?

489
00:57:04.850 --> 00:57:07.310
Him? There's nothing
for him to do.

490
00:57:08.200 --> 00:57:10.422
The Rojos threatened
to kill his little boy Jesus,

491
00:57:10.543 --> 00:57:12.792
and he was forced
to accept things.

492
00:57:15.661 --> 00:57:17.618
That Ramon is smart.

493
00:57:19.586 --> 00:57:21.466
Where are you going?

494
00:57:25.373 --> 00:57:27.481
To the Rojos
to look for a job.

495
00:57:33.666 --> 00:57:36.103
I am glad we have the
<i>americano</i> with us.

496
00:57:36.282 --> 00:57:38.750
It's the best thing that could
have happened to us, you know,

497
00:57:39.118 --> 00:57:42.120
'cause if either government
starts an inquiry,

498
00:57:42.187 --> 00:57:44.188
we'll need every man
we can get.

499
00:57:45.657 --> 00:57:49.246
I guess you know to be at war
with the Baxters now,

500
00:57:49.316 --> 00:57:51.167
is worse than sitting
on a big case of dynamite.

501
00:57:51.260 --> 00:57:54.189
Where should we put this?
Put it over there.

502
00:58:02.023 --> 00:58:04.403
Come on, everybody!
Drink up!

503
00:58:36.175 --> 00:58:38.676
Good shooting.
Very good shooting.

504
00:58:38.842 --> 00:58:40.945
When you want to kill a man,
you must shoot for his heart.

505
00:58:41.013 --> 00:58:43.762
And the Winchester
is the best weapon.

506
00:58:43.915 --> 00:58:46.878
That's very nice,
but I'll stick with my .45.

507
00:58:47.792 --> 00:58:50.955
When a man with a .45
meets a man with a rifle,

508
00:58:51.123 --> 00:58:54.352
the man with the pistol
will be a dead man.

509
00:58:54.961 --> 00:58:57.936
That's an old Mexican proverb,
and it's true.

510
00:58:59.364 --> 00:59:00.982
You believe that?

511
00:59:02.767 --> 00:59:05.972
Paquito, take five men and escort
Marisol to the small house.

512
00:59:06.066 --> 00:59:08.172
And stay there till I return.

513
00:59:17.282 --> 00:59:19.959
Everything's prepared.
Do not be worried.

514
00:59:20.586 --> 00:59:22.419
I will return tomorrow.

515
00:59:22.655 --> 00:59:24.363
All the wagons are ready.
We can leave.

516
00:59:24.457 --> 00:59:28.557
Everyone, enjoy yourselves
during my absence.

517
00:59:46.061 --> 00:59:48.629
You heard Ramon.
Let's have a good time.

518
00:59:56.998 --> 01:00:00.723
<i>~ Do you remember</i>
<i>sweet Becky from Pike ~</i>

519
01:00:01.143 --> 01:00:04.167
<i>~ She roamed the world</i>
<i>with her lover Ike ~</i>

520
01:00:04.880 --> 01:00:06.908
<i>~ Ike and Betsy ~</i>

521
01:00:07.149 --> 01:00:08.916
<i>~ Betsy from Pike ~</i>

522
01:00:12.414 --> 01:00:14.054
He weighs over a ton.

523
01:00:14.218 --> 01:00:16.631
Of course, with all he
poured into himself.

524
01:01:34.102 --> 01:01:35.102
Papa,

525
01:01:36.438 --> 01:01:39.472
did you not tell me
no one could go see Mama?

526
01:01:41.042 --> 01:01:42.517
That's right.

527
01:01:43.033 --> 01:01:45.680
Then why does that man see her
when I cannot?

528
01:01:49.318 --> 01:01:52.186
- I want Mama.
- Go away from the door.

529
01:01:52.254 --> 01:01:55.192
Quiet! Quiet.
We cannot show ourselves.

530
01:01:55.290 --> 01:01:57.658
You must remember that.
You must stay away.

531
01:02:08.570 --> 01:02:09.905
Hello.

532
01:02:30.175 --> 01:02:32.143
There's somebody shooting
up at the small house.

533
01:02:32.211 --> 01:02:35.324
Saddle the horses immediately!
Come on. Let's go!

534
01:03:03.542 --> 01:03:05.265
Look out!

535
01:03:52.753 --> 01:03:54.768
Here you are.
Now, take this money.

536
01:03:55.447 --> 01:03:58.611
It's enough to live on for a while.
Now, get across the border.

537
01:03:58.780 --> 01:04:01.466
Get as much distance between
yourselves and San Miguel as possible.

538
01:04:01.533 --> 01:04:03.694
How may we thank you
for what you are doing?

539
01:04:04.631 --> 01:04:07.771
Don't try. Just get going
before the Rojos get here.

540
01:04:11.988 --> 01:04:13.761
Why do you do this for us?

541
01:04:15.244 --> 01:04:18.415
Why? 'Cause I knew
someone like you once.

542
01:04:18.524 --> 01:04:20.885
There was no one there
to help. Now, get moving.

543
01:04:23.983 --> 01:04:25.693
Get moving.

544
01:04:26.654 --> 01:04:28.434
Get out of here!

545
01:05:10.835 --> 01:05:13.064
What do you see, Chico?

546
01:05:13.204 --> 01:05:16.227
They're all dead.
They massacred them.

547
01:05:16.708 --> 01:05:18.289
They kidnapped Marisol!

548
01:05:18.570 --> 01:05:20.280
This looks like
the work of the Baxters.

549
01:05:20.512 --> 01:05:23.814
Quick, let's get back before
they attack our house and the town.

550
01:07:19.014 --> 01:07:21.590
Chico,
give out the ammunition.

551
01:07:21.749 --> 01:07:25.620
Esteban, spread your men around the house.
Keep your eyes open.

552
01:07:25.720 --> 01:07:28.782
Miguel, Paco, Vincente,
Martin, behind the house.

553
01:07:28.857 --> 01:07:32.507
Manolo and Alvaro,
come with me. Stay alert.

554
01:07:32.765 --> 01:07:36.607
The way they killed the men in the small
house, there must be a lot of them.

555
01:07:44.423 --> 01:07:46.357
It's a warm evening.

556
01:07:49.911 --> 01:07:54.576
One of our wagons lost a wheel, so we
had to turn back here to get help.

557
01:07:56.134 --> 01:07:58.559
One of the men tells me,

558
01:07:59.379 --> 01:08:02.308
the Baxters
attacked the small house.

559
01:08:03.808 --> 01:08:05.681
Do you know about it?

560
01:08:09.266 --> 01:08:11.023
Tell me what you know.

561
01:08:31.402 --> 01:08:32.506
Well?

562
01:08:33.865 --> 01:08:35.572
Where did you hide Marisol?

563
01:08:38.551 --> 01:08:39.675
Rubio.

564
01:09:05.620 --> 01:09:08.234
You are thirsty.
You want to drink?

565
01:09:09.054 --> 01:09:11.959
No, no,
it is too soon to drink.

566
01:09:15.637 --> 01:09:17.514
Bring him over here!

567
01:09:46.261 --> 01:09:47.928
You are behaving
like a stubborn idiot.

568
01:09:48.085 --> 01:09:50.514
Tell us where Marisol is,
and it will all be ended!

569
01:09:50.709 --> 01:09:51.849
In a week,
you'll be back in shape.

570
01:09:51.917 --> 01:09:54.574
You'll get out and you can go
wherever you want.

571
01:10:06.214 --> 01:10:07.905
That's enough for today.

572
01:10:08.850 --> 01:10:12.122
Sooner or later, he'll talk.
It's just a matter of time.

573
01:10:12.920 --> 01:10:15.870
Watch out he doesn't escape or die.
Otherwise, do as you like.

574
01:10:20.626 --> 01:10:24.351
But wait till he comes to.
This way, he hardly feels anything.

575
01:10:56.565 --> 01:10:59.025
I've had a poker hand waiting
for me for three days.

576
01:10:59.212 --> 01:11:02.609
Now I'm stuck here! I can't get to it
while I'm guarding this <i>americano</i> idiot!

577
01:11:02.750 --> 01:11:04.671
I think you will find this
more amusing than cards.

578
01:11:04.788 --> 01:11:07.057
All orders are to be sure
he does not die,

579
01:11:07.125 --> 01:11:10.715
and also make sure he regrets
the day he was born.

580
01:11:12.542 --> 01:11:15.003
The gringo is asleep,
I imagine.

581
01:11:15.149 --> 01:11:18.142
That's all right.
I'll enjoy waking him up.

582
01:12:22.006 --> 01:12:25.286
- Esteban, what was that noise?
- I do not know.

583
01:12:25.450 --> 01:12:27.535
I heard a yell,
and then a crash.

584
01:12:59.654 --> 01:13:01.588
It's useless to hide.

585
01:13:03.724 --> 01:13:05.840
You're finished playing
the smart boy.

586
01:13:07.662 --> 01:13:09.596
Go up
and look in the loft.

587
01:13:11.158 --> 01:13:13.337
And take a look
behind the barrels!

588
01:13:25.146 --> 01:13:26.691
Let's get out of here!

589
01:13:37.093 --> 01:13:39.436
Hurry! Quick!

590
01:13:39.576 --> 01:13:43.489
Hurry with that water!
Hey, you, come with me!

591
01:13:57.578 --> 01:14:01.177
Surround the town! Block all
the streets leading out!

592
01:14:01.315 --> 01:14:03.250
Find him for me!

593
01:14:04.619 --> 01:14:07.720
Esteban, search the whole town.
Follow me!

594
01:14:09.089 --> 01:14:12.750
Get him back right now!
You've got to at any cost!

595
01:14:12.826 --> 01:14:16.639
Look in the stables, in every
corral, in the storeroom!

596
01:14:16.733 --> 01:14:18.467
Look for him in the church!

597
01:14:18.677 --> 01:14:21.251
Go in there!
Search every inch of it!

598
01:14:21.319 --> 01:14:24.909
Search everywhere!
Rubio, in here!

599
01:14:25.682 --> 01:14:28.470
If somebody is hiding
him, burn their house down,

600
01:14:28.611 --> 01:14:30.157
and kill them like dogs!

601
01:14:30.672 --> 01:14:32.289
You, up here!

602
01:14:32.596 --> 01:14:36.436
Look for him near the Baxters, but
take him alive! I want him alive!

603
01:14:36.740 --> 01:14:38.168
Alive!

604
01:14:39.809 --> 01:14:42.363
Rubio, in the bar.

605
01:15:12.819 --> 01:15:16.039
He says he knows nothing.
He's trying to be smart.

606
01:15:16.107 --> 01:15:17.716
Bring him here to me.

607
01:15:19.871 --> 01:15:21.839
I swear,
I'm telling the truth.

608
01:15:22.144 --> 01:15:25.119
Well,
you know nothing, huh?

609
01:15:26.126 --> 01:15:29.875
- Nothing. I've not seen him.
- Rubio, you take care of him.

610
01:16:11.319 --> 01:16:13.062
Where have you hidden him?

611
01:16:14.565 --> 01:16:17.467
I didn't...

612
01:16:21.955 --> 01:16:25.071
You're the right friend
for that filthy <i>americano</i>.

613
01:16:25.235 --> 01:16:27.060
And you'll end up
the same way.

614
01:16:28.257 --> 01:16:29.803
We looked everywhere.

615
01:16:30.131 --> 01:16:32.896
In his cellar, in the attic,
on the roof.

616
01:16:33.013 --> 01:16:35.005
But there is no trace.

617
01:16:35.309 --> 01:16:37.371
I couldn't find anybody there
in the back room.

618
01:16:37.464 --> 01:16:40.340
I'm certain he has taken
refuge with the Baxters.

619
01:16:40.580 --> 01:16:42.080
The <i>americano</i> isn't stupid.

620
01:16:42.197 --> 01:16:44.727
He knows that that's the
best place for him to hide.

621
01:16:47.181 --> 01:16:49.061
The Baxters, eh?

622
01:16:50.326 --> 01:16:51.943
Then better go and get him.

623
01:16:56.511 --> 01:16:58.315
And that's for
being his friend.

624
01:17:33.129 --> 01:17:34.511
Curse them.

625
01:17:40.767 --> 01:17:42.126
Piripero.

626
01:17:42.477 --> 01:17:43.695
Eh?

627
01:17:50.981 --> 01:17:52.129
Piripero.

628
01:18:03.913 --> 01:18:06.397
- Come here.
- I can't see anybody.

629
01:18:07.685 --> 01:18:08.786
Come here.

630
01:18:09.536 --> 01:18:11.012
<i>Dios mio!</i>

631
01:18:18.532 --> 01:18:20.430
What are you doing in there?

632
01:18:21.930 --> 01:18:23.826
Never mind.
Get me out of here.

633
01:18:24.413 --> 01:18:26.545
But you're not dead yet.

634
01:18:26.709 --> 01:18:29.283
I will be if you don't get
me out of here, quick.

635
01:18:29.427 --> 01:18:30.785
Get that lid down.

636
01:19:57.820 --> 01:19:58.828
Rubio.

637
01:20:20.873 --> 01:20:22.865
I see some signs of life.

638
01:20:23.825 --> 01:20:26.285
Let's be ready
when they decide to come out.

639
01:20:30.760 --> 01:20:33.103
Don't shoot!
We surrender!

640
01:20:33.173 --> 01:20:34.438
Don't shoot!

641
01:20:35.680 --> 01:20:39.686
Stop! Don't shoot!
We're coming out!

642
01:20:42.380 --> 01:20:45.941
- I'm surrendering! Hold back your fire!
- Don't shoot!

643
01:20:46.035 --> 01:20:47.956
We're surrendering!

644
01:21:17.030 --> 01:21:18.342
Stop.

645
01:21:19.185 --> 01:21:21.083
I wanna take a look at this.

646
01:22:57.300 --> 01:23:01.403
Ramon, don't shoot!
We're coming out!

647
01:23:04.774 --> 01:23:06.438
We surrender!

648
01:23:06.576 --> 01:23:09.414
Listen, you've won.
It's enough!

649
01:23:09.648 --> 01:23:12.080
I'll get out of town!
I'll do whatever you like!

650
01:23:12.178 --> 01:23:14.755
- You promise that?
- I swear it, Ramon!

651
01:23:15.385 --> 01:23:17.590
You won't try a trick
of any kind?

652
01:23:17.720 --> 01:23:20.214
None! No, no tricks!

653
01:23:20.356 --> 01:23:22.885
I said before, I give you my word.
We'll leave!

654
01:23:22.978 --> 01:23:26.657
Are you sure? You had better
ask permission of your wife.

655
01:23:28.343 --> 01:23:30.382
Maybe she won't be too happy!

656
01:23:43.923 --> 01:23:45.213
Antonio!

657
01:23:46.805 --> 01:23:47.812
John!

658
01:24:12.692 --> 01:24:14.192
Murderers.

659
01:24:15.925 --> 01:24:17.870
They had no guns.

660
01:24:18.479 --> 01:24:21.478
Murderers!
I hope you rot in hell!

661
01:24:21.548 --> 01:24:23.938
May you and your brothers
die spitting blood!

662
01:24:24.008 --> 01:24:25.367
Curse you for this!

663
01:24:26.140 --> 01:24:27.897
Murderers!

664
01:24:50.341 --> 01:24:52.964
Let's go.
The show's over, anyway.

665
01:24:57.253 --> 01:25:00.860
Keep looking for him.
Search among those bodies.

666
01:25:01.157 --> 01:25:03.424
The filthy <i>americano</i>
has to be somewhere!

667
01:27:22.582 --> 01:27:23.982
Silvanito?

668
01:27:28.771 --> 01:27:30.424
Where's Silvanito?

669
01:27:33.892 --> 01:27:35.576
Any news today?

670
01:27:35.836 --> 01:27:38.513
I have to tell you
some news that's pretty bad.

671
01:27:38.580 --> 01:27:42.349
I hate to tell you this, Joe, but...
Where is Silvanito?

672
01:27:43.544 --> 01:27:47.714
Silvanito, he was captured this
morning by those men of Ramon's.

673
01:27:47.972 --> 01:27:50.853
They grabbed him outside the village.
He was on his way to this mine.

674
01:27:50.927 --> 01:27:53.962
He was bringing in some provisions.
Ramon's got him now.

675
01:27:54.133 --> 01:27:56.101
He's being tortured,
but he won't talk.

676
01:27:56.195 --> 01:27:58.093
I know him well.
He's a stubborn man.

677
01:27:58.233 --> 01:28:02.170
No matter what they do, he won't say
a word, even if it means his life.

678
01:28:02.263 --> 01:28:05.273
Listen to me. They'll never
be able to force him.

679
01:28:16.602 --> 01:28:19.974
Now, old fool,
loosen up your tongue.

680
01:28:23.209 --> 01:28:25.527
No.
Rubio!

681
01:28:27.679 --> 01:28:30.148
You better get back
to your shop, old man.

682
01:28:30.306 --> 01:28:33.118
- You're liable to have some business.
- Very good!

683
01:28:33.185 --> 01:28:35.120
That's what
I wanted to hear.

684
01:28:35.202 --> 01:28:38.423
And I have a little surprise
for you that I brought along.

685
01:28:38.576 --> 01:28:40.191
I know how much
you are going to need it.

686
01:28:40.259 --> 01:28:42.160
It was very hard
to get my hands on it.

687
01:28:42.254 --> 01:28:46.697
But I got it by first using my head.
No one can resist two barrels of wine.

688
01:28:46.916 --> 01:28:49.376
Isn't that right?
Then I thought that,

689
01:28:49.493 --> 01:28:53.204
well, you might need that pistol,
and I brought another present.

690
01:28:54.940 --> 01:28:58.911
It's dynamite.
I stole it from the Rojos.

691
01:28:59.378 --> 01:29:00.578
And now it seems to me

692
01:29:00.646 --> 01:29:03.480
the moment's come
for you to light the fuse

693
01:29:03.621 --> 01:29:05.378
and send it back to them.

694
01:29:25.081 --> 01:29:26.603
Still lots of light.

695
01:29:30.409 --> 01:29:33.069
Too early to be asleep, yet.

696
01:29:37.216 --> 01:29:38.669
Rubio, here.

697
01:29:44.356 --> 01:29:48.693
I shouldn't like to ruin the rifle.
I could never find another like this.

698
01:29:50.196 --> 01:29:52.936
Listen, Ramon, let's try it
with this one now.

699
01:31:58.156 --> 01:31:59.916
Gringo!

700
01:32:06.710 --> 01:32:08.444
Heard you wanted
to see me.

701
01:32:09.951 --> 01:32:11.911
The <i>americano</i>'s dead.

702
01:32:13.668 --> 01:32:15.506
Let the old man down.

703
01:32:33.575 --> 01:32:35.620
What's wrong, Ramon?

704
01:32:36.674 --> 01:32:38.525
You losing your touch?

705
01:32:46.922 --> 01:32:48.341
Are you afraid, Ramon?

706
01:32:51.994 --> 01:32:54.456
You shoot to kill,
you better hit the heart.

707
01:32:56.494 --> 01:32:58.415
Your own words, Ramon.

708
01:33:14.791 --> 01:33:16.408
The heart, Ramon.

709
01:33:16.900 --> 01:33:18.653
Don't forget the heart.

710
01:33:21.974 --> 01:33:24.982
Aim for the heart
or you'll never stop me.

711
01:35:01.406 --> 01:35:05.020
When a man with a .45
meets a man with a rifle,

712
01:35:05.629 --> 01:35:08.089
you said the man
with the pistol's a dead man.

713
01:35:09.167 --> 01:35:11.041
Let's see if that's true.

714
01:35:35.190 --> 01:35:37.444
Go ahead, load up and shoot.

715
01:37:42.918 --> 01:37:44.728
Hey, listen, Joe.

716
01:37:45.153 --> 01:37:48.406
Listen, Joe, I... I...

717
01:37:49.648 --> 01:37:52.178
Oh, Joe, Joe.

718
01:38:24.157 --> 01:38:27.929
Well, guess your government will
be glad to see that gold back.

719
01:38:28.597 --> 01:38:32.779
And you, you don't want to be
here when they get it, eh?

720
01:38:34.669 --> 01:38:37.511
You mean, the Mexican
government on one side,

721
01:38:37.773 --> 01:38:40.065
and maybe the Americans
on the other side?

722
01:38:40.409 --> 01:38:42.243
Me, right smack in the middle?

723
01:38:43.954 --> 01:38:45.446
Too dangerous.

724
01:38:47.148 --> 01:38:49.881
- So long.
- <i>Adiós</i>.

725
01:38:56.000 --> 01:39:56.000
<b><font color="#ff0000">Subtittled By
TONY JAIMY</font></b>
